For the convenience of the reader, we finish by stating a universal property of the Day convolution, that, combined with symmetric monoidal localizations, is useful for constructing symmetric monoidal maps of form $\Pc_{?}(\Sch^?, \Sp) \to \Pc_{?}(\Sch^?, \Sp)$ in $\Pr^L$. The statement is a special case of \cite[Proposition~4.8.1.10]{HA}. 

Given an $\infty$-category $\Cc$, we denote by $\Pc_\Kc(\Cc)$ the $\infty$-category obtained by freely adjoining $\Kc$-indexed colimits to $\Cc$ \cite[\S 5.3.6]{HTT}. Recall that if $\Cc$ is a symmetric monoidal $\infty$-category, then we say that the symmetric monoidal structure is \emph{compatible with $\Kc$-indexed colimits}.

\begin{prop}
Let $\Cc$ be a symmetric monoidal $\infty$-category, and let $\Kc$ be a collection of simplicial sets. Then, there is a unique symmetric monoidal structure on $\Pc_\Kc(\Cc)$ that is characterized by the following conditions
\begin{enumerate}
\item the Yoneda embedding $j \colon \Cc \to \Pc_\Kc(\Cc)$ is symmetric monoidal;

\item the symmetric monoidal structure on $\Pc_\Kc(\Cc)$ is compatible with $\Kc$-indexed colimits.
\end{enumerate}
Furthermore, if $\Dc$ is a symmetric monoidal category whose symmetric monoidal structure is compatible with $\Kc$-indexed colimits, then the restriction functor induces an equivalence of categories
\[
\Fun_{\Kc}^\otimes(\Pc_\Kc(\Cc), \Dc) \xto{\sim} \Fun^\otimes(\Cc, \Dc)
\]
from $\Kc$-indexed colimit preserving symmetric monoidal functors from $\Pc_\Kc(\Cc)$ to symmetric monoidal functors from $\Cc$.
\end{prop}


