\textbf{Steering Strength $\bm{\delta_t}$ Configuration:}  Another key hyperparameter in KDS is the {steering strength}, denoted as $\delta_t$. During the diffusion process, the sampling procedure exhibits varying sensitivity to guidance. Specifically, at later stages of the sampling process (i.e., smaller $t$ values, approaching the data), the model can be more sensitive. To ensure stability and effective guidance, we define $\delta_t$ conditionally based on the timestep $t$. Assuming $T$ is the total number of diffusion steps, we set:
\begin{equation}
    \delta_t = \begin{cases}
0 & \text{if } t/T < 0.3 \\
0.3 & \text{if } t/T \ge 0.3
\end{cases}
\label{eq:delta_t}
\end{equation}

Note that, this hyperparameter setting is fixed for all the experiments across different applications and backbones.

