\begin{lem}\label{lem:KernelOfAlphaGeneratedByMeridians}
    The kernel $K$ of the natural pushforward map $$\pi_1(\Sg\setminus\{x_1,\ldots,x_{n-1}\},x_n)\to\pi_1(\Xg\setminus\{x_1,\ldots,x_{n-1}\},x_n)$$ is precisely the subgroup generated by simple loops that bound an embedded disk (which is normal by Lemma \ref{lem:conjugate}).
