\begin{proposition}
The axioms in Theorems \ref{theorem:lex-cel} and \ref{theorem:plurality} are logically independent.  \end{proposition}


\section{Conclusion}
\label{section:conclusion}

This study examines SRSs in terms of independence axioms. We provide new characterizations of lex-cel $R^{L}$ (Theorem \ref{theorem:lex-cel}) and plurality $R^{P}$ (Theorem \ref{theorem:plurality}) by substituting the independence axioms in the existing characterization of IIS $R^{IIS}$. Our results reveal the characteristics of these three SRSs in terms of alternative combinations of independence axioms and shed new insight on their fundamental connections. 

