The analysis described here uses a partial pathway summation approach to capture quantum interference in the effective coupling between initial and final states~\cite{mattuck1992guide}. This strategy allows dissection of  electronic, vibronic, and driving force effects on the transfer rates. 
Using this approach, we provide a unified framework to describe ET/EnT rates  in  multi-acceptor systems~\cite{phelan2019quantum,phelan2019quantum1,fisher2023fundamental,fisher2024long}.
