\subsection{Reaction coordinate correlation}
\label{sec:model-vibration}
%Now that we have the language for discussing the multi-acceptor systems, we dissect multi-acceptor electron transfer problem by describing various possible cases, focusing on the correlation of vibrations between the acceptors.
Using the model Hamiltonian in Eqs.~\eqref{eq:hamiltonian}-\eqref{eq:hamiltonian-nuclei-3}, we study the influence of correlated reaction coordinate motions on ET/EnT reactions with two acceptors. We explore four kinds of  reaction coordinate correlation (Fig.~\ref{fig:illustration}).
